a typical training week varies each  month depending on what phase of the  season we're in but more or less we have  two relatively easy days a week which  usually consists of cruise run and an  easy swim the other days of the week  consists of two hard runs too hard bike  workouts and then two hard swims it's  taken me a really long time to figure  out my nutrition as an athlete you  really need to understand that you're  feeling to perform prior to using  science and sport and race I really  struggle on the run whether it was from  a lack of nutrition or from stomach  issues from other products race day and  training don't vary too much especially  on high-intensity days I really rely on  the science and sport isotonic gels to  get me through hard sessions because  that's the only thing my stomach can  handle when I'm putting out a really  solid effort during some of my easier  sessions I like to have the science and  sport go energy bars and then after  every training session I have at least a  scoop or two of rego recovery and I feel  really helps me recover faster or just  get in a few extra calories between  sessions so that I can train to the best  of my ability  [Music]
 

